##  Runtime and Memory Analysis

| **Data Structure** | **Average Search Time** | **Average Insert Time** | **Memory Efficiency** | **Notes** |
|---------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------|------------------------|------------|
| **Vector** | O(n) | O(1) | Moderate | Must iterate through all elements for searches. |
| **Hash Table** | O(1) average, O(n) worst | O(1) | High | Collisions can affect performance and require extra handling. |
| **Binary Search Tree (BST)** | O(log n) average | O(log n) | High | Provides ordered traversal and efficient searching. |

---

##  Recommendation
After analyzing performance and memory characteristics, the **Binary Search Tree (BST)** was selected for implementation in Project Two.  

While the hash table offers slightly faster average lookups, the BST’s advantage lies in its **ability to maintain sorted data** and efficiently support **in-order traversal**—ideal for printing the course list in alphanumeric order.  
It also provides predictable performance for both insertion and search, making it the most balanced and readable structure for this problem.

